{
  "id": "22178_hinpatsusuru",
  "headword": "{頻発|ひんぱつ}する",
  "reading": "ひんぱつする",
  "romaji": "hinpatsusuru",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb (intransitive)",
  "gloss": "to occur frequently; to happen repeatedly",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to occur frequently; to happen repeatedly",
      "explanation": "For events, especially undesirable ones like accidents, crimes, or problems, to happen with high frequency. Almost always used for negative occurrences."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "22178_hinpatsusuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{交通|こうつう}{事故|じこ}が{頻発|ひんぱつ}している。",
      "english": "Traffic accidents are occurring frequently.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22178_hinpatsusuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{地域|ちいき}では{空|あ}き{巣|す}が{頻発|ひんぱつ}している。",
      "english": "Burglaries are occurring frequently in this area.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "22178_hinpatsusuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "システムエラーが{頻発|ひんぱつ}しているため、{原因|げんいん}を{調査|ちょうさ}する{必要|ひつよう}がある。",
      "english": "System errors are occurring frequently, so it's necessary to investigate the cause.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Almost exclusively used for negative events — accidents, crimes, errors, natural disasters. Rarely used for positive occurrences. Common in news reporting.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {事故|じこ}が{頻発|ひんぱつ}する — accidents occur frequently\n- {犯罪|はんざい}が{頻発|ひんぱつ}する — crimes occur frequently\n- {地震|じしん}が{頻発|ひんぱつ}する — earthquakes occur frequently\n- トラブルが{頻発|ひんぱつ}する — troubles occur frequently\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {多発|たはつ}する — to occur frequently; similar meaning but slightly less emphasis on the rapidity\n- {相次|あいつ}ぐ — to happen one after another; emphasizes the sequential, unrelenting nature\n- {繰|く}り{返|かえ}す — to repeat; neutral, can be used for any type of event",
